# ============================================================
# Repo-root guard.
#
# web/.gitignore and demo/.gitignore cover most of this already, but
# demo/.gitignore ignores itself (it is just `*`), so a fresh clone loses
# that protection and a rebuilt demo/ becomes committable. These rules
# survive cloning.
# ============================================================

# ---- NEVER COMMIT: these are the answer key in usable form ----
# demo/index.html embeds every slug with its real/fake type.
# web/facilitator/ holds the answer key, print manifest and QR codes.
demo/
web/facilitator/

# ---- build output; regenerate with `npm run build` ----
web/dist/

# ---- local only ----
web/node_modules/
web/.cert/
node_modules/

# ---- editor / OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ============================================================
# DELIBERATELY TRACKED, AND WHY THE REPO MUST STAY PRIVATE
#
#   web/cards.json           every headline with its real/fake verdict
#   supabase/seed-cards.sql  the same content, generated
#
# Both are build inputs, so they have to be in the repo — and both are
# the game's answer key in plain text. If this repository is ever made
# public, the game is over for anyone who reads it.
#
# If it must go public: remove those two files from history, keep them
# out of the repo, and build/deploy from a local copy instead.
# ============================================================
